messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 175 and 934? Please reason step by step.', "<think>.\nTo find the product of 175 and 934, we can use the distributive property of multiplication over addition. This means we can break down the multiplication into smaller parts and then add the results together.\n\nFirst, let's express 934 as a sum of two numbers that are easier to work with. We can write 934 as 900 + 30 + 4. Now, we can use the distributive property to multiply 175 by each of these numbers separately:.\n\n1. Multiply 175 by 900:.\n   \\[.\n   175 \\times 900 = 175 \\times (9 \\times 100) = (175 \\times 9) \\times 100.\n   \\].\n   To find \\(175 \\times 9\\), we can use the fact that \\(175 \\times 9 = 175 \\times (10 - 1) = 175 \\times 10 - 175 \\times 1 = 1750 - 175 = 1575\\). So,.\n   \\[.\n   175 \\times 900 = 1575 \\times 100 = 157500.\n   \\].\n\n2. Multiply 175 by 30:.\n   \\[.\n   175 \\times 30 = 175 \\times (3 \\times 10) = (175 \\times 3) \\times 10.\n   \\].\n   To find \\(175 \\times 3\\), we can use the fact that \\(175 \\times 3 = 525\\). So,.\n   \\[.\n   175 \\times 30 = 525 \\times 10 = 5250.\n   \\].\n\n3. Multiply 175 by 4:.\n   \\[.\n   175 \\times 4 = 700.\n   \\].\n\nNow, we add the results of these three multiplications together:.\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
