messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 271 and 797? Please reason step by step.', "<think>.\nTo find the product of 271 and 797, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's how it works:.\n\n1. Write down the numbers one below the other, aligning them by their place values:.\n   ```.\n     271.\n   x 797.\n   ```.\n\n2. Multiply each digit of the bottom number (797) by the top number (271), starting from the rightmost digit:.\n   - Multiply 7 by 271: \\(7 \\times 271 = 1897\\).\n   - Multiply 9 by 271: \\(9 \\times 271 = 2439\\).\n   - Multiply 7 by 271: \\(7 \\times 271 = 1897\\).\n\n3. Write these products below the line, aligning them by their place values:.\n   ```.\n     271.\n   x 797.\n   ----.\n    1897.\n   2439.\n   1897.\n   ----.\n   ```.\n\n4. Add the products together, starting from the rightmost column:.\n   - Add the last column: \\(7 + 9 + 7 = 23\\). Write down 3 and carry over 2.\n   - Add the next column: \\(1 + 3 + 7 + 2 = 13\\). Write down 3 and carry over 1.\n   - Add the next column: \\(2 + 9 + 1 + 1 = 13\\). Write down 3 and carry over 1.\n   - Add the leftmost column: \\(2 + 7 + 2 = 11\\). Write down 1 and carry over 1.\n\n5. Combine the results from each column, including the carryovers:.\n   ```.\n     271.\n   x 797.\n   ----.\n    1897.\n   2439.\n   1897.\n   ----.\n   216667.\n   ```. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
