messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 628 and 561? Please reason step by step.', "<think>.\nTo find the product of 628 and 561, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's how we do it step by step:.\n\n1. **Multiply the ones place of the second number (6) by each digit in the first number (628), starting from the rightmost digit.**.\n   - \\(6 \\times 8 = 48\\).\n   - \\(6 \\times 2 = 12\\).\n   - \\(6 \\times 6 = 36\\).\n\n2. **Write down the results of these multiplications, aligning them according to their place values.**.\n   - \\(48\\) (ones place).\n   - \\(12\\) (tens place).\n   - \\(36\\) (hundreds place).\n\n3. **Add a zero at the end of the second row because we are multiplying by the tens place of the second number.**.\n   - \\(120\\) (tens place).\n   - \\(360\\) (hundreds place).\n\n4. **Multiply the tens place of the second number (6) by each digit in the first number (628), starting from the rightmost digit.**.\n   - \\(6 \\times 8 = 48\\).\n   - \\(6 \\times 2 = 12\\).\n   - \\(6 \\times 6 = 36\\).\n\n5. **Write down the results of these multiplications, aligning them according to their place values.**.\n   - \\(48\\) (ones place).\n   - \\(12\\) (tens place).\n   - \\(36\\) (hundreds place).\n\n6. **Add a zero at the end of the second row because we are multiplying by the hundreds place of the second number.**.\n   - \\(120\\) (tens place).\n   - \\(360\\) (hundreds place).\n\n7. **Multiply the hundreds place of the second number (6) by each digit in the first number (628), starting from the rightmost digit.**.\n   - \\(6 \\times 8 = 48\\).\n   - \\(6 \\times 2 = 12\\).\n   - \\(6 \\times 6 = 36\\).\n\n8. **Write down the results of these multiplications, aligning them according to their place values.**.\n   - \\(48\\) (ones place).\n   - \\(12\\) (tens place).\n   - \\(36\\) (hundreds place).\n\n9. **Add a zero at the end of the second row because we are multiplying by the thousands place of the second number.**.\n   - \\(120\\) (tens place).\n   - \\(360\\) (hundreds place).\n\n10. **Add all the rows together to get the final product.**.\n    - \\(48\\) (ones place).\n    - \\(120\\) (tens place).\n    - \\(360\\) (hundreds place).\n    - \\(1200\\) (tens place).\n    - \\(3600\\) (hundreds place).\n    - \\(4800\\) (thousands place).\n\n11. **Combine all the results to get the final product.**.\n    - \\(360000\\) (thousands place).\n    - \\(36000\\) (hundreds place).\n    - \\(1200\\) (tens place).\n    - \\(48\\) (ones place).\n\n12. **Add all the results together to get the final product.**. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
