messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 689 and 922? Please reason step by step.', "<think>.\nTo find the product of 689 and 922, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's how it works:.\n\n1. Write down the numbers one below the other, aligning them by their place values:.\n   ```.\n     689.\n   x 922.\n   ```.\n\n2. Multiply 689 by the units digit of 922 (which is 2):.\n   ```.\n     689.\n   x   2.\n   ----.\n     1378.\n   ```.\n\n3. Multiply 689 by the tens digit of 922 (which is 2), but remember to shift the result one position to the left because we're dealing with tens:.\n   ```.\n     689.\n   x  20.\n   ----.\n    13780.\n   ```.\n\n4. Multiply 689 by the hundreds digit of 922 (which is 9), and shift the result two positions to the left:.\n   ```.\n     689.\n   x 900.\n   ----.\n   620100.\n   ```.\n\n5. Add all the partial products together:.\n   ```.\n     1378.\n   +13780.\n   +620100.\n   ----.\n   620100.\n   ```. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
