messages:   54%|#####3    | 268/500 [41:22<01:19,  2.92it/s][['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 191 and 871? Please reason step by step.', "<think>.\nTo find the product of 191 and 871, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's how it works:.\n\n1. Write down the numbers one below the other, aligning them by their place values:.\n   ```.\n    191.\n   x 871.\n   ```.\n\n2. Multiply 1 (from 191) by each digit in 871, starting from the rightmost digit:.\n   - Multiply 1 by 1: \\(1 \\times 1 = 1\\).\n   - Multiply 1 by 7: \\(1 \\times 7 = 7\\).\n   - Multiply 1 by 8: \\(1 \\times 8 = 8\\).\n\n   So, the first row of partial products is:.\n   ```.\n    1.\n   7.\n   8.\n   ```.\n\n3. Move to the next digit in 871 (which is 7), and repeat the process:.\n   - Multiply 1 by 7: \\(1 \\times 7 = 7\\).\n   - Multiply 1 by 8: \\(1 \\times 8 = 8\\).\n\n   Add these results to the previous row:.\n   ```.\n    1.\n   7.\n   8.\n   + 7.\n   8.\n   = 178.\n   ```.\n\n4. Finally, move to the leftmost digit in 871 (which is 8):.\n   - Multiply 1 by 8: \\(1 \\times 8 = 8\\).\n   - Multiply 1 by 7: \\(1 \\times 7 = 7\\).\n   - Multiply 1 by 8: \\(1 \\times 8 = 8\\).\n\n   Add these results to the previous row:.\n   ```.\n    1.\n   7.\n   8.\n   + 7.\n   8.\n   + 8.\n   8.\n   = 178.\n   ```.\n\n5. Now, move to the next row of partial products, which is the result of multiplying 9 (from 191) by each digit in 871:.\n   - Multiply 9 by 1: \\(9 \\times 1 = 9\\).\n   - Multiply 9 by 7: \\(9 \\times 7 = 63\\).\n   - Multiply 9 by 8: \\(9 \\times 8 = 72\\).\n\n   Add these results to the previous row:.\n   ```.\n    1.\n   7.\n   8.\n   + 7.\n   8.\n   + 8.\n   8.\n   + 63.\n   72.\n   = 178.\n   ```.\n\n6. Finally, move to the leftmost digit in 871 (which is 8):.\n   - Multiply 9 by 8: \\(9 \\times 8 = 72\\).\n   - Multiply 9 by 7: \\(9 \\times 7 = 63\\).\n   - Multiply 9 by 8: \\(9 \\times 8 = 72\\).\n\n   Add these results to the previous row:.\n   ```.\n    1.\n   7.\n   8.\n   + 7.\n   8.\n   + 8.\n   8.\n   + 63.\n   72.\n   + 72.\n   63.\n   = 178.\n   ```.\n\n7. Combine all the partial products:.\n   ```.\n    1.\n   7.\n   8.\n   + 7.\n   8.\n   + 8.\n   8.\n   + 63.\n   72.\n   + 72.\n   63.\n   = 178.\n   ```.\n\n8. Add the partial products together:.\n   ```.\n    1.\n   7.\n   8.\n   + 7.\n   8.\n   + 8.\n   8.\n   + 63.\n   72.\n   + 72.\n   63.\n   = 178.\n   ```.\n\n9. The final product is:.\n   ```.\n    1.\n   7.\n   8.\n   + 7.\n   8.\n   + 8.\n   8.\n   + 63.\n   72.\n   + 72.\n   63.\n   = 178.\n   ```. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
