o the next digit in the second number (783), which is 7 (hundreds place):**.\n   - Multiply 7 (the hundreds place of 783) by 2 (the ones place of 982): \\(7 \\times 2 = 14\\). Write down 4 in the hundreds place of the result and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n   - Multiply 7 (the hundreds place of 783) by 8 (the tens place of 982): \\(7 \\times 8 = 56\\). Add the carried over 1: \\(56 + 1 = 57\\). Write down 7 in the tens place of the result and carry over 5 to the thousands place.\n   - Multiply 7 (the hundreds place of 783) by 9 (the hundreds place of 982): \\(7 \\times 9 = 63\\). Add the carried over 5: \\(63 + 5 = 68\\). Write down 68 in the thousands place of the result.\n\n   So far, the partial product looks like this:.\n   ```.\n     982.\n   x 783.\n   ------.\n     246.\n    240.\n   292.\n   ------.\n    7856.\n   ```.\n\n4. **Add the partial products together:**.\n   ```.\n     982.\n   x 783.\n   ------.\n     246.\n    240.\n   292.\n   ------.\n    7856.\n   ```. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
