messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 767 and 688? Please reason step by step.', "<think>.\nTo find the product of 767 and 688, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's how we do it step by step:.\n\n1. **Multiply the ones place of the second number (8) by each digit in the first number (767), starting from the rightmost digit:**.\n   - \\(8 \\times 7 = 56\\).\n   - \\(8 \\times 6 = 48\\).\n   - \\(8 \\times 7 = 56\\).\n\n   So, the result of multiplying the ones place of 688 by 767 is 5648.\n\n2. **Multiply the tens place of the second number (8) by each digit in the first number (767), starting from the rightmost digit:**.\n   - \\(8 \\times 6 = 48\\).\n   - \\(8 \\times 7 = 56\\).\n   - \\(8 \\times 7 = 56\\).\n\n   So, the result of multiplying the tens place of 688 by 767 is 4856.\n\n3. **Multiply the hundreds place of the second number (6) by each digit in the first number (767), starting from the rightmost digit:**.\n   - \\(6 \\times 7 = 42\\).\n   - \\(6 \\times 6 = 36\\).\n   - \\(6 \\times 7 = 42\\).\n\n   So, the result of multiplying the hundreds place of 688 by 767 is 4236.\n\n4. **Add all the results together:**.\n   - \\(5648\\) (from the ones place).\n   - \\(4856\\) (from the tens place).\n   - \\(4236\\) (from the hundreds place).\n\n   Adding these together gives us:.\n   \\[.\n   5648 + 4856 + 4236 = 14730.\n   \\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
