messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 678 and 358? Please reason step by step.', "<think>.\nTo find the product of 678 and 358, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's how we do it step by step:.\n\n1. **Multiply the ones place of the second number (8) by each digit in the first number (678), starting from the rightmost digit and moving left.**.\n   - \\(8 \\times 8 = 64\\).\n   - \\(8 \\times 7 = 56\\).\n   - \\(8 \\times 6 = 48\\).\n\n2. **Write down the results of these multiplications, aligning them according to their place values.**.\n   - \\(64\\) (ones place).\n   - \\(56\\) (tens place).\n   - \\(48\\) (hundreds place).\n\n3. **Move to the next digit in the second number (5) and repeat the process.**.\n   - \\(5 \\times 8 = 40\\).\n   - \\(5 \\times 7 = 35\\).\n   - \\(5 \\times 6 = 30\\).\n\n4. **Add a zero at the end of the second row of results because we are multiplying by the tens place.**.\n   - \\(40\\) (tens place).\n   - \\(35\\) (hundreds place).\n   - \\(30\\) (thousands place).\n\n5. **Move to the next digit in the second number (3) and repeat the process.**.\n   - \\(3 \\times 8 = 24\\).\n   - \\(3 \\times 7 = 21\\).\n   - \\(3 \\times 6 = 18\\).\n\n6. **Add a zero at the end of the third row of results because we are multiplying by the hundreds place.**.\n   - \\(24\\) (hundreds place).\n   - \\(21\\) (thousands place).\n   - \\(18\\) (ten-thousands place).\n\n7. **Add all the rows together, carrying over any excess to the next column.**.\n   - \\(64\\) (ones place).\n   - \\(560\\) (tens place).\n   - \\(4800\\) (hundreds place).\n   - \\(400\\) (thousands place).\n   - \\(350\\) (ten-thousands place).\n   - \\(180\\) (hundred-thousands place).\n\n8. **Summing up all the columns:**.\n   - \\(64 + 560 + 4800 + 400 + 350 + 180 = 6454\\). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
